# armour/shared/pauldron_plate_r: the medium plate pauldron on the right shoulder (plate.3; P2c slice, re-shaded by
# LADDER-ARMOUR, STYLE_P2 25.6 / 27.5): a cop and one lame, 2 px past the shoulder line; the cop lit at its top-left
# (step 3, one step-4 ridge pixel = its glint), the rest steps 2 and 1, the lame's lit edge one row of step 2. Near side over
# the arm, far side behind it; it rides the lean and the bob and lifts a pixel on wind-ups (`up`).
# Finish regions: R the lame's hem, P the cop's face, N the seam between cop and lame, W a spot on the shadow side.
# Shared by the man and the woman (D10). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# (LADDER-ARMOUR alloys i1) a step-4 specular on the lit top of the first scales / lames / plates (top-left light):
# with no step 4 a coloured alloy read as clay; the glint and the dark core make any metal read as metal.
use person
role pauldron plate.3
layer armNear
anchor shoulderR
keys pauld
z 5
side R
# (FORGE-MANTLE, round 2) `when shoulder-plate replace` views: the BROAD mass drawn for the forge styles (STYLE_P2 28.3; generated by FORGE-MANTLE gen.py from shapes5.py); 0-forge looks keep the base views.

